UNIT binding_of
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY package
ANCHOR rederive@9e2245be5f42 cli/lsp/analyze.mjs bindingOf, with boundSha from cli/sir/v05.mjs (over parse from cli/sir/sir-parse.mjs), canonicalText and sha256 from cli/sir/sir-parse.mjs and legacyPrintSha from the frozen cli/sir/legacy-print.mjs; the code is the truth, accidents included
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG binding_of(lang_text: text, primary_text: text | none) -> record[status: text, bound: text | none, primarySha: text | none]
ENVELOPE lang_text is any well-formed text; primary_text is any well-formed text or none. Nothing in scope throws. Text
  holding an unpaired surrogate code unit is outside the abstract text type; OUT-OF-DOMAIN 1-2 state what the package does
  with it, and the js language file widens its envelope to cover those cases.
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION Report whether a SIR v0.5 language file is bound to its primary (SIR v0.5 section 23b): the language file
  declares PRIMARY-SHA256 followed by a hash, and the binding holds when that hash is the SHA-256 of the primary's
  canonical text. The result is a record: status (one of ok, stale, legacy, unbound, no-primary), bound (the 64 hex digits
  found in the language file, or none) and primarySha (the primary's canonical-text hash, or none). A hash written before
  2026-10-26 hashed the old canonical print instead; it is recognized as legacy. The review and the editor both report
  bindings with it.
NOTE Rust is omitted. Cause: domain — the review system ships as JavaScript (rdv review and the rederive/sir-review GitHub
  Action); there is no Rust consumer.
BEHAVIOR
R1 BOUND is read through the parser. Cut lang_text into lines as R3 does (CRLF, lone CR, lone LF; U+FEFF removed from the
  leading run; trailing spaces and tabs dropped) but keep every line as it then is (no dropping, no re-indenting), and
  classify each line by TABLE PARSE-LINE. D = the FIRST line classified DIRECTIVE whose NAME is PRIMARY-SHA256. bound is
  none when there is no D. Otherwise bound = the ARGUMENT of D when both hold, and none when either fails: (a) the
  ARGUMENT is exactly 64 characters of LOWER-HEX; (b) every non-empty line after D, up to the next DIRECTIVE line or the
  end, is a COMMENT. Only the first D counts: a later PRIMARY-SHA256 directive never rescues or overrides it. The ARGUMENT
  is D's text after its NAME, cut before its comment marker (the first number sign with a space or tab before it and a
  space, a tab or the line end after it), then stripped of spaces and tabs at both ends; an attribute (CITED, EARNED or
  ANCHOR), a second word or any other character leaves it not 64 hex digits. A hash on the next line, a 65th digit, a
  suffix, uppercase hex, an NBSP or U+2028 separator, an attribute or a continuation line all give none CITED FIDELITY package
R2 STATUS, decided in TABLE STATUS order; the first matching row wins. bound is computed before any row and is reported
  in every row as R1 found it.
R3 CANONICAL TEXT (the binding normal form). Cut the text into lines at every CRLF pair, every lone CR and every lone LF
  (a CR directly followed by LF is one break). For each line: delete every U+FEFF inside the line's leading run of
  characters drawn from space, tab and U+FEFF (U+FEFF elsewhere stays); then drop trailing spaces and tabs; a line now empty
  is dropped; a line that begins with spaces or tabs has that whole run replaced by exactly two spaces. Every other
  character is kept as it is (U+00A0, U+3000, U+2028 and comment text included). The kept lines are joined with LF and
  followed by one LF; no kept line gives the empty text.
R4 HASH. A hash is SHA-256 (FIPS 180-4) over the UTF-8 encoding of a text, written as 64 lowercase hex digits.
R5 primarySha = the hash (R4) of the canonical text (R3) of primary_text (OUT-OF-DOMAIN 1 is the one case where it is
  none although primary_text is text).
R6 LEGACY HASH = the hash (R4) of the LEGACY PRINT of primary_text, where the legacy print comes from the LEGACY PARSE.
  LEGACY PARSE: cut primary_text at every LF only (a CR is not a break); from each piece remove one trailing CR when it
  ends with one; walk the pieces in order with a CURRENT entry (none at the start) and classify each by TABLE LEGACY-LINE.
  INDENT is a piece's leading run of spaces and tabs; CONTENT is the rest.
R7 LEGACY PRINT: one line per entry in entry order, the entry's NAME, then a space and its ARGS when ARGS is not empty,
  then for every attribute in its order a space, the keyword, a space and the value (an empty value leaves the line ending
  in that space); after it, one line per continuation in order, two spaces then the continuation. Lines are joined with LF
  and followed by one LF; no entry gives the text of one LF CITED FIDELITY package
R8 TRAILING COMMENT CUT, applied to CONTENT (giving CODE): find the smallest index j such that the characters before j
  hold no LINE-BREAK, the character at j is in SPACE, the next is the number sign, the one after that is absent or in SPACE,
  and the characters from j+2 to the end hold no LINE-BREAK. When found, CODE = CONTENT before j with its trailing SPACE
  members removed; otherwise CODE = CONTENT. So a line-break character inside CONTENT blocks the cut unless that very
  character is the space before the number sign CITED FIDELITY package
R9 HEAD of a column-0 CODE: CODE splits into NAME and REST only when CODE is not empty and its first character is not in
  SPACE: NAME = the longest leading run of characters outside SPACE, then the run of SPACE members after it is skipped,
  REST = what remains, and REST must hold no LINE-BREAK. Otherwise (empty CODE, a first character in SPACE such as U+00A0 or
  U+FEFF, or a line break in REST) CODE has no head. A NAME made of DIRECTIVE-NAME followed by one colon loses the colon.
  The head is a directive when NAME (after that) is a DIRECTIVE-NAME CITED FIDELITY package
R10 ATTRIBUTES of a piece s (REST of a directive line, or CODE of an indented line), giving a BODY and attributes in found
  order: repeatedly take the LEFTMOST start i of a run of SPACE members such that the run (all of it), then one KEYWORD,
  then a second run of one or more SPACE members, then a VALUE reach the end of s, where VALUE is one or more characters
  holding no LINE-BREAK. The second run is as long as possible while leaving a valid VALUE; when s ends in that run the
  VALUE is its last character, so the run must be at least two characters long and that last character not a LINE-BREAK.
  Each find records the keyword with the VALUE stripped of SPACE members at both ends (repeating a keyword within one piece
  appends with one space unless the earlier value is empty, which is replaced), and s is cut to its characters before i;
  stop when nothing is found. BODY = what is left, stripped of SPACE members at both ends. Without a line break in s at most
  one attribute is found, and it takes everything after its keyword (later keywords included) CITED FIDELITY package
R11 MERGE across lines: a directive's attributes start as those of its own line; an indented continuation's attributes
  overwrite same-keyword values (the earlier value is lost) and a keyword new to the entry is added after the existing ones;
  a keyword already present keeps its position CITED FIDELITY package
R12 KEPT, declared (architect ruling 2026-11-02, F7 and F8). (a) A legacy binding survives every edit the legacy print
  cannot see: comment lines, trailing comments, lines made only of SPACE members, lines before the first entry, and an
  attribute value overwritten by R11; so legacy does not mean unchanged since binding (the review flags every status
  other than ok). (b) The hash of the empty text is ok for every primary whose canonical text is empty (empty, or only
  blank lines), and the hash of the one-LF text is legacy for every primary whose legacy parse yields no entry (only
  comments, or only text before any directive) CITED FIDELITY package
NOTE Kept, declared (architect ruling 2026-11-02, F6): the package guards the legacy-hash computation with a catch that no
  text input reaches, since the legacy parse and print never fail on text. It is not observable and need not be reproduced.
TABLE STATUS — first matching row wins; bound per R1; L = the legacy hash of R6
  primary_text is none                         | status no-primary, primarySha none
  bound is none                                | status unbound, primarySha per R5
  bound equals primarySha                      | status ok, primarySha per R5
  primarySha is not none and bound equals L   | status legacy, primarySha per R5
  otherwise                                    | status stale, primarySha per R5
TABLE PARSE-LINE — first matching row wins, per line of R1 (the live parser's tolerant reading)
  empty                                                                              | blank (ignored)
  after its leading spaces and tabs it begins with the number sign                   | COMMENT
  begins with a space or tab                                                         | CONTINUATION
  NAME, the text before its first space or tab (the whole line when it has none), with one final colon removed when what precedes it is a DIRECTIVE-NAME other than CITED, is a DIRECTIVE-NAME other than CITED | DIRECTIVE
  otherwise (CITED x, CITED: x, a lowercase word, a name glued to its text by U+00A0, U+3000 or U+2028, a line led by U+00A0) | CONTINUATION
TABLE LEGACY-LINE — first matching row wins, per piece of R6
  every character of the piece is in SPACE, or it is empty                           | skipped
  CONTENT begins with the number sign                                                | dropped (a comment; CURRENT unchanged)
  INDENT empty and CODE (R8) has a head (R9) that is a directive                     | a new entry: NAME, ARGS = BODY and attributes of R10 on REST; it becomes CURRENT
  INDENT empty, no directive, CURRENT exists                                         | CODE itself, unstripped and with no attribute split, appended as a continuation of CURRENT
  INDENT empty, no directive, no CURRENT                                             | dropped
  INDENT not empty, no CURRENT                                                       | dropped
  INDENT not empty, CURRENT exists                                                   | R10 on CODE: attributes merged by R11, BODY (possibly empty) appended as a continuation
PINNED charset SPACE = U+0009 U+000A U+000B U+000C U+000D U+0020 U+00A0 U+1680 U+2000..U+200A U+2028 U+2029 U+202F U+205F U+3000 U+FEFF CITED R8 R9 R10 and TABLE LEGACY-LINE row 1 — every whitespace test of the LEGACY parse (R1 and R3 use only space and tab)
PINNED charset LINE-BREAK = U+000A U+000D U+2028 U+2029 CITED R8 R9 R10 — the characters a single-line scan of the legacy parse cannot cross
PINNED charset LOWER-HEX = U+0030..U+0039 U+0061..U+0066 CITED R1 (a) — uppercase hex never binds
PINNED grammar DIRECTIVE-NAME = one ASCII uppercase letter, then zero or more of ASCII uppercase letters, ASCII digits and hyphen CITED R9 and TABLE PARSE-LINE — R1, R12 and ABC-123 qualify; unknown names are directives too
PINNED grammar KEYWORD = CITED | EARNED | ANCHOR CITED R10 — case-sensitive
OUT-OF-DOMAIN what the package does with an unpaired surrogate code unit (reproduced; the js-only oracle verifies it).
  1. In primary_text: canonical text is refused and primarySha is none. The STATUS rows still run in order with that none:
  no-primary only when primary_text is none, unbound when bound is none, and otherwise stale, never ok and never legacy
  (the legacy row needs a primarySha) CITED FIDELITY package
  2. In lang_text: no effect of its own; an unpaired surrogate is not LOWER-HEX and is content to TABLE PARSE-LINE.
INVARIANT status ok implies bound equals primarySha and primarySha is not none; status no-primary implies primarySha none;
  status unbound implies bound none. Formatting-only edits of R3 (line endings, U+FEFF marks in a leading run, trailing
  spaces and tabs, blank lines, indentation width or style) never change status ok.
ORACLE value -> oracles/binding_of.json  CANONICAL-SHA256 d762b0da5a1e61d9d63de6a8a5af9fb838f3b5ff87b77084a2db69d0e9bc1dcc
SCOPE IN: the bound reading through the parser, the status order, canonical text with its surrogate refusal, SHA-256, the legacy parse and
  print. OUT: how the review and the editor render a status; reading files.
PROVENANCE rederive@9e2245be5f42 cli/lsp/analyze.mjs bindingOf (safeSha), cli/sir/v05.mjs boundSha, cli/sir/sir-parse.mjs parse,
  canonicalText, sirLines and sha256, cli/sir/legacy-print.mjs legacyPrintSha (parse in legacy mode and print, frozen as of rederive 20bdd3dd041a).
  Cut cold 2026-11-02 by the sighted decomposer on c509956a8f8a, revised the same day on 9e2245be5f42 (architect rulings F1-F5); seeds from packages/colors/sir/strip and the lab's is_number family.
